A||N||6||fastback87||3 EEPROM questions||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-21-2001||03:19 PM||||1.  does anyone know of any difference in the stock programming between an 85 v6 auto eeprom and an 87 v6 auto eeprom?  I have an 87 gt and was wondering if they changed anything for the worse to meet emissions in 87.  <P>2.  I was also wondering if anyone could give me some info on where to buy a eeprom programmer for that chip and possibly others.  <P>3.  Is there a user friendly chip upgrade program?  that allows you to change performance type stuff?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-21-2001||06:01 PM||||The Fiero ECM doesn't use EEPROM... It's UV erasable EPROM. I'm not aware of an EEPROM or a Flash part that is pin compatible with the 2764 and 27128 EPROM parts. Just which one you need I don't know on the V6.<P>There are a number of places to get EPROM programmers and erasers. You can even build them. Try JDR.com and other electronics supliers online.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||AJ88||11-21-2001||07:11 PM||||Have a look at the PROM board on <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/techboard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/techboard</A> <P>It's Firebird/Camaro stuff, but these guys know what they are talking about!<P>Before you post anything, read 'Traxions Introduction Article' from the link at the top of the page, and you might find what you are looking for.  They aren't too interested in answering the same newbie questions over and over.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>AFAIK, the 29256 Flash chips will work, you just need to 'double up' the bin file.  Traxion's article explains all that.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fastback87||11-22-2001||12:02 AM||||so is the chip reprogramable or not?||||reg||9
Z||000004||terryk||11-22-2001||12:26 PM||||Yes, it's just that some early one's used OTP (One Time Programmable - no way to erase them) chips so you may have to get some eproms.||||reg||1
Z||000005||newfie||11-23-2001||09:38 AM||||I'm planning on making a system that will read from the ALDL and be able to make changes to the computer on the fly.  This will be part of my turbocharging project.  I plan on either replacing the UV prom with EEPROM.  And possibling using RAM once the car is running to make any changes.  I haven't thouroughly thought it out yet but its an idea.  It'll be programed via Laptop. ||||reg||1
